#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166867 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166720 :question/id #uuid "58850b39-db80-532d-9f60-808a215da76c" :question/math-academy-id "e-9579" :question/problem "![](images/a9/a92eae1ab0af29ea895b570c95199ece1e292c09953ebb2dabbb7c6e2d422d6c.png)\n\nFind $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}$ for the right-opening parabola shown above." :question/worked-solution "The diagram shows that the parabola has its vertex at $O,$ and passes through the point $(3,-2).$\n\nThe standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(0,0)$ is given by\n\n$$\ny^2 = 4px.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x = 3$ and $y = -2$ into the equation above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-2)^{2} & =4p(3) \\\\ 4 & =12p \\\\ p & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of our parabola is \n\n$$\ny^2 = \\dfrac{4}{3}x.\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate $\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{4}{3}x) \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2}{3y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "53a1649d-4279-5b7c-839c-728f333b2c3f" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049118 :topic/difficulty 0.7541705546563298 :topic/encompasses [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186428110 :encompassing/rationale "Initial Codex estimate from captured target-band crossing frequency. Selected account foundations: 1 rises / 3 eligible passed source activities = 0.333333; nearest selected fraction = 1/3. Crossing activity numbers [1]; waits [1]. Separate account estimates: foundations=1/3 (1/3). Selection: most observations, then lower weight, then account name; no averaging. Single-activity estimates included. Intervening target updates: True. Crossing frequency is the chosen practical estimate of encompassing coverage; a multi-band rise counts once. This does not interpret color steps as physical repetition units. Method: encompassing-report.md. Evidence: reference/mathacademy/encompassing-analysis-2026-10-11/frequency-fractions/foundations-frequency-estimates.json, pair 1124->2978. All account evidence retained in the prepared import's selected-relationships.json." :encompassing/topic {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049178} :encompassing/weight 0.3333333333333333}] :topic/id #uuid "dc0c57dc-d0cc-5d0f-bc3f-5c52faa2e959" :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096702} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096703} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096704} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096705}] :topic/math-academy-id 1124 :topic/next [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048350} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048559} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048894} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049336} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049506} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050769} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051063}] :topic/title "Left and Right Opening Parabolas"}] :knowledge-point/level-coverage [{:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186550211 :question-generator/id #uuid "e359bb2a-e736-568f-8841-85888e3467e5" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186166867.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167095 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d0573536-31f0-563b-9d07-911863e634bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{y}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163649} {:answer/id #uuid "d09192f8-b86c-51d6-a122-7afcd699607f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163650} {:answer/id #uuid "d9efdc1d-d656-5d1e-83d6-ccd7d0ea85d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163651} {:answer/id #uuid "f4600882-36d2-52ce-8da2-b54d8b2af6df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163652} {:answer/id #uuid "2e3b5a55-f245-5539-8b5a-59cf6f8686da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163653}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d9efdc1d-d656-5d1e-83d6-ccd7d0ea85d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163651} :answer-field/id #uuid "41202eeb-84d9-576f-9f59-f15c773b23c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163648}] :question/id #uuid "0981d1d8-5908-5954-92c8-10f4e8de0d4e" :question/math-academy-id "q-127372" :question/problem "![](images/00/0030e466a772b1ccd61140453c5e0e50ff365a0bf42034422bce9e1691983c43.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ for the right-opening parabola shown above." :question/worked-solution "The right-opening parabola has vertex $(0,0)$ and passes through $(1,2)$. Its equation is $y^2=4x$. Differentiate to obtain $2yy'=4$, so $$\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac2y$$ for $y\\ne0$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167096 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b50d0c40-6788-57f6-abfc-e79bf313d479" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{y}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163655} {:answer/id #uuid "0872fa03-25f1-5ab1-8e8a-b7add5e28113" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163656} {:answer/id #uuid "40308631-4569-53b4-a049-a0c1e9473978" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163657} {:answer/id #uuid "515e1940-de9b-5005-bcc4-522fce4979f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163658} {:answer/id #uuid "77251aea-0d1b-53cd-8e9c-1840b159150c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163659}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40308631-4569-53b4-a049-a0c1e9473978" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163657} :answer-field/id #uuid "106254b3-fb7a-53e5-9145-bedbc3b56b87" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163654}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2b2fc0d7-ecff-5b63-8ad8-a6faaff8e7b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-127374" :question/problem "![](images/88/88bec66b7ece961f2f0fc4083ce317f2bdc414e0a219d61bbf9bf73ae667ca0f.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the left-opening parabola shown above." :question/worked-solution "The diagram shows that the parabola has its vertex at $O,$ and passes through the point $(-2,2).$\n\nThe general equation of a left- or right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(0,0)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=-2$ and $y=2$ into the equation above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2)^{2} & =4p(-2) \\\\ 4 & =-8p \\\\ p & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of our parabola is \n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=-2x.\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-2x) \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{1}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262782 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "219845eb-d05c-53b6-8c35-514bf8a6a3e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260163} {:answer/id #uuid "2cbaa061-8eee-52ef-b708-518d83dacbe3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260277} {:answer/id #uuid "6a53e920-1f56-54ef-9a0d-a07c822f8f3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{6y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260807} {:answer/id #uuid "6f270028-5c9b-5ad1-bf83-211b5d81af31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260852} {:answer/id #uuid "d675cc22-4e88-5836-a463-6a2f29d37cb6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261761}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2cbaa061-8eee-52ef-b708-518d83dacbe3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260277} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ac39f57-fa34-5bb6-bec8-a47660173164" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262255}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d5970e3a-67be-579a-8f6a-680fce2bb7ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-127510" :question/problem "![](images/e0/e0d18f7db92cfbe372f998e69d2395f2d586eb36cd25773588149c4ccf678eba.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the right-opening parabola shown above." :question/worked-solution "The diagram shows that the parabola has its vertex at $O,$ and passes through the point $(3,6).$\n\nThe standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(3,6)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=3$ and $y=6$ into the equation above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(6)^{2} & =4p(3) \\\\ 36 & =12p \\\\ p & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of our parabola is \n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=12x.\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(12x) \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =12 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{6}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262787 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53b126be-2e72-5683-87f0-2bce708ce0b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260580} {:answer/id #uuid "ac29313d-f700-5356-b3ea-db25827d7000" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261378} {:answer/id #uuid "af2deb81-9196-5179-b2ff-4e88fe6ffef3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261420} {:answer/id #uuid "c2ee63f7-23d8-539c-8477-779c46a531e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261595} {:answer/id #uuid "d1164fca-4cb8-5220-a316-6ca8fe78ed20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261719}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "53b126be-2e72-5683-87f0-2bce708ce0b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260580} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c21556d-ce63-50ba-aa4c-f313d47a9e13" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262257}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b2ff195e-41e9-5105-9c9e-ed134d28a53d" :question/math-academy-id "q-127515" :question/problem "![](images/5e/5eedb15e515993bdc8a2ee37ab4c7c0e0225b9d2118d5d60e8593de5ea56f199.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the left-opening parabola shown above." :question/worked-solution "The diagram shows that the parabola has its vertex at $O,$ and passes through the point $(-1,2).$\n\nThe general equation of a left- or right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(0,0)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=-1$ and $y=2$ into the equation above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2)^{2} & =4p(-1) \\\\ 4 & =-4p \\\\ p & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of our parabola is \n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=-4x.\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-4x) \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-4 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{2}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262788 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05cc5c38-3fac-504b-a52a-dbbcc512e957" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259926} {:answer/id #uuid "46b94c76-6f4b-5df7-afa2-245210c1a600" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260489} {:answer/id #uuid "5ac2c1f5-97e4-55ee-8c09-94a6ec7fc43d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260651} {:answer/id #uuid "7dc8ab5c-9f98-553d-8e5c-4e7a8e4f49d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260970} {:answer/id #uuid "aa32c440-9d05-5e9e-95fc-705f2a3492a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261364}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "46b94c76-6f4b-5df7-afa2-245210c1a600" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260489} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb45d64f-7844-5746-b5c9-fba237c20fd2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262562}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "72fb768f-c740-5cf4-b10e-4551f1d715de" :question/math-academy-id "q-127520" :question/problem "![](images/60/60987d053d138d4a26cbc05adccb0da23810f97243f9399d3fe401a0202394b0.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the left-opening parabola shown above." :question/worked-solution "The diagram shows that the parabola has its vertex at $O,$ and passes through the point $(-8,4).$\n\nThe general equation of a left- or right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(0,0)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=-8$ and $y=4$ into the equation above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4)^{2} & =4p(-8) \\\\ 16 & =-32p \\\\ p & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of our parabola is \n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=-2x.\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-2x) \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{1}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297360 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18f6ba14-67bb-52a5-83f3-90748a808eb7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{49}{10y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295413}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "18f6ba14-67bb-52a5-83f3-90748a808eb7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{49}{10y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295413} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ea47b69-ba23-5df0-89cb-9a0a8a5b3195" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296865}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2b5b23fa-be02-551f-968d-c9191c07be80" :question/math-academy-id "q-312780" :question/problem "![](images/b2/b269001ff5a3a1a1d86125157ee2f5b77d89ebcf0041f8d403dbc931b796c5e8.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the right-opening parabola shown above. Express the answer in terms of the variable $y.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The diagram shows that the parabola has its vertex at $O,$ and passes through the point $(5,7).$\n\nThe standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(0,0)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=5$ and $y=7$ into the equation above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(7)^{2} & =4p(5) \\\\ 49 & =20p \\\\ p & =\\frac{49}{20}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of our parabola is \n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=\\frac{49}{5}x.\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{49}{5}x) \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{49}{5} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{49}{10y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317217 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08ce1afa-8b88-5a8a-8cdc-4e464a1bb102" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{6y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315162}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08ce1afa-8b88-5a8a-8cdc-4e464a1bb102" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{6y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315162} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ad31bfe-fcf5-5162-a8e6-4281f1f124b2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316722}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "28f921c8-6fd7-5d79-b2ff-0d1df567197f" :question/math-academy-id "q-342215" :question/problem "![](images/c4/c403f11093b76facafbecb72bcc413640ac67fe6ed73d6b64374230f39e29aba.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the left-opening parabola shown above. Express the answer in terms of the variable $y.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The diagram shows that the parabola has its vertex at $O,$ and passes through the point $(-3,-1).$\n\nThe general equation of a left- or right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(0,0)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=-3$ and $y=-1$ into the equation above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1)^{2} & =4p(-3) \\\\ 1 & =-12p \\\\ p & =-\\frac{1}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of our parabola is \n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=-\\frac{1}{3}x.\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\frac{1}{3}x) \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{1}{6y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317218 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ad5bf0a8-9d5e-50fe-96f9-d4d663d3f517" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316094}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad5bf0a8-9d5e-50fe-96f9-d4d663d3f517" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316094} :answer-field/id #uuid "12408f4c-1370-5d9b-b3b2-f660b8736202" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316591}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a43aa514-b6a3-516e-bf25-cd1e713491f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-342218" :question/problem "![](images/73/7367cb4ae1feb4e18b98b712687ceb4a1db67f8c9e4965af3ffd1253a827f346.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the left-opening parabola shown above. Express the answer in terms of the variable $y.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The diagram shows that the parabola has its vertex at $O,$ and passes through the point $(-6,6).$\n\nThe general equation of a left- or right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(0,0)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=-6$ and $y=6$ into the equation above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{6}^{2} & =4p(-6) \\\\ 36 & =-24p \\\\ p & =-\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of our parabola is \n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=-6x.\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-6x) \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-6 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{3}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317243 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4203b15d-0bea-5e2b-934d-26d20084a739" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315503}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4203b15d-0bea-5e2b-934d-26d20084a739" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315503} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd3bd66b-afeb-5b87-8ae5-7c88b3e0adad" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317149}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3b67c83b-c5b3-5c60-b778-f810479299ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-342354" :question/problem "![](images/85/85d75e0f3a9f2a30282d1f1754b0c46da49e8f73ff2a858c856ba5492eb21cca.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the right-opening parabola shown above. Express the answer in terms of the variable $y.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The diagram shows that the parabola has its vertex at $O,$ and passes through the point $(8,-8).$\n\nThe standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(0,0)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=8$ and $y=-8$ into the equation above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-8)^{2} & =4p(8) \\\\ 64 & =32p \\\\ p & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of our parabola is \n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=8x.\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(8x) \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =8 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{4}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$