:db/id #edb/ref 17592186550171} {:answer/id #uuid "28b78bcf-a12c-569a-bb17-9e66db7be89e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550173} {:answer/id #uuid "6dcfe650-ba97-586c-9fa2-c5fd10d5d462" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550182} {:answer/id #uuid "a77383dc-b83a-560c-83e8-3d350ee2aea0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550190} {:answer/id #uuid "af1c4627-36c6-5ae9-993e-1728a7e2772f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550191}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a77383dc-b83a-560c-83e8-3d350ee2aea0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550190} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4a49c6e-ae2b-5f68-b70a-03e4f0368e1c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550193}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8f4d582e-5489-5989-8e7a-5c782843e1d4" :question/problem "![](images/a7/a7c56fd2bfe1aa346bcebdf79f128140235c69fd72cf5b147eace57827fe9689.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the left-opening parabola shown above." :question/worked-solution "The diagram shows that the parabola has its vertex at $O,$ and passes through the point $(-6,-3).$\n\nThe general equation of a left- or right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(0,0)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=-6$ and $y=-3$ into the equation above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-3)^{2} & =4p(-6) \\\\ 9 & =-24p \\\\ p & =-\\frac{3}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of our parabola is \n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=-\\frac{3}{2}x.\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\frac{3}{2}x) \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{3}{4y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186550198 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "57e246f3-cb19-54af-a1b3-e2c195a5e06e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550177} {:answer/id #uuid "5e758806-41e5-566a-bd49-b8b45956c8f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550178} {:answer/id #uuid "7a61b366-e9b7-591e-8aa3-cb81c88d5dc9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550184} {:answer/id #uuid "e2d2e80c-ed1d-537f-9327-a685067c2765" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550204} {:answer/id #uuid "f437c276-f770-525e-91cd-572b961b92ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4y}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550210}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7a61b366-e9b7-591e-8aa3-cb81c88d5dc9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550184} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7e14ab2-deee-519b-b7a6-3593e9d0bdd8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550197}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cd0c7321-e023-5633-bdad-071f1a7eccfc" :question/problem "![](images/00/0012f2c4830f5acc401b551e8421b0bbb730c2e27f68010a691d74dcfd6ea93a.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the right-opening parabola shown above." :question/worked-solution "The diagram shows that the parabola has its vertex at $O,$ and passes through the point $(6,-3).$\n\nThe standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(0,0)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=6$ and $y=-3$ into the equation above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-3)^{2} & =4p(6) \\\\ 9 & =24p \\\\ p & =\\frac{3}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of our parabola is \n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=\\frac{3}{2}x.\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{3}{2}x) \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{3}{4y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186550201 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53593d78-cb2e-5976-b61a-00fc854f664f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550176} {:answer/id #uuid "68a12903-3439-50f4-80b6-1bf16f06ff09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550180} {:answer/id #uuid "bb62951c-7be2-5985-89a7-796fe92d0fe7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550194} {:answer/id #uuid "d2f3ef9c-8be7-525c-bc57-d1ce7659ff00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550200} {:answer/id #uuid "f14e21d6-640a-5340-bceb-b2ba5f8abe44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{y}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550208}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "68a12903-3439-50f4-80b6-1bf16f06ff09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550180} :answer-field/id #uuid "f232da10-2779-54d0-8c60-da3948a8ec17" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550209}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d4eb74b6-db84-5116-8322-9b24d0326181" :question/problem "![](images/03/03a879d7f79141f6816bf74a73efa87b089e2c213bc2b58bc93727cd8ee08500.png)\n\nThe parabola shown above has equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=8x.\n$$\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the right-opening parabola shown above." :question/worked-solution "The equation of our parabola is \n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=8x.\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(8x) \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =8 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{4}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186550203 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2894d3a0-b026-5675-b147-35e34dd8a2d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550172}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2894d3a0-b026-5675-b147-35e34dd8a2d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550172} :answer-field/id #uuid "94b609e7-041d-52dc-a078-56c86fba7886" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550189}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "dcf749a6-fb83-5c81-b302-2511741ae8e2" :question/problem "![](images/19/19065a69504e6bd90d36a7804f05ce9952a90c838c1ddb43c374e53ccbf038a7.png)\n\nThe parabola shown above has equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=1x.\n$$\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the right-opening parabola shown above. Express the answer in terms of the variable $y.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The equation of our parabola is \n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=1x.\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1x) \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{2y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186656935 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "010e431e-2442-595f-b58f-7395c7a2ac4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{y}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186656387} {:answer/id #uuid "49bbf2de-9d18-5871-b538-74cfe0a7c8ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186656488} {:answer/id #uuid "8971c208-368c-5b93-8184-03df20eae652" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186656592} {:answer/id #uuid "c14c54d0-314d-5621-bdd4-18d15e6b3bee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{y}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186656670} {:answer/id #uuid "ebf236bc-0c37-5680-868d-81f9aab6d958" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186656730}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8971c208-368c-5b93-8184-03df20eae652" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186656592} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1ed141e-2053-5309-a1a8-f4c6aea7a6e3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186656827}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ba669e01-0424-5360-b582-c8ddd3a27bb6" :question/math-academy-id "q-127507" :question/problem "![](images/0f/0fb6e28df6459782453b94a7516d47407e3625fc13609ab2b85e7e5e2ac597f4.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the right-opening parabola shown above." :question/worked-solution "The diagram shows that the parabola has its vertex at $O,$ and passes through the point $(2,4).$\n\nThe standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(0,0)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=2$ and $y=4$ into the equation above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4)^{2} & =4p(2) \\\\ 16 & =8p \\\\ p & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of our parabola is \n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=8x.\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(8x) \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =8 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{4}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent to a Parabola"}]}
